From e9eeb0721369866dd521e9359a3af7ebcc53b0fd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HempFiend <17104973+jaidenscool1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 15:53:13 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Blaze 3.x: Madden 25 logs in (Nucleus OAuth +
 Authentication2) and reaches its main menu

- heat2 maps go out sorted by key (strings case-insensitively): Blaze 3.x clients binary-search
  them, so Madden couldn't find preAuth CONF keys we sent and crashed formatting a null string
  (PPU 0x961554). Test: "map keys sorted".
- preAuth CONF gives heat2 clients nucleusConnect (our HTTP server), blazeServerClientId and
  identityRedirectUri. Madden GETs <nucleusConnect>/connect/auth with its PSN ticket; the HTTP
  server swaps the ticket for a one-time code (NucleusAuth) and redirects; Authentication2 (35)
  login (10) with that code runs the PS3 login (Ps3LoginHandler.Login, split out of ps3Login).
- OSDKSettings group SG_MATCHUP with Madden's match-type views (QM_STD ... CS_MUTDT); a missing
  view crashed at 0x14fa760.

Madden now passes login, the online bootstrap and a tuning-data notice to its main menu. NHL 15 is
unchanged (still reaches its online menus). docs/EA-Sports-Blaze3-heat2.md section 6b.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
