+## 6b. Madden NFL 25 — Nucleus login, sorted maps, SG_MATCHUP (reaches its main menu, 2026-11-13)
+
+The "FGGameSim crash ~52 s" was never an emulator bug: it is the same thread crashing (PC `0x961554`)
+0.5 s after the Blaze session starts, and the time only looked fixed because Madden used to connect then.
+Madden's BlazeSDK 13.3 differs from NHL's 3.19 in three ways the server now handles (uscl-blaze 0016):
+
+1. **Sorted maps (all heat2 clients).** Blaze 3.x decodes TDF maps into sorted vector maps and looks keys
+   up by **binary search** (`0xa37b74`), so map entries must go out in key order (case-insensitive for
+   strings). Our encoder sent dictionary order, so Madden's preAuth `CONF` lookups failed for keys we *did*
+   send. `Heat2Writer.WriteMap` sorts now (test: "map keys sorted").
+2. **Nucleus OAuth login.** After preAuth Madden builds
+   `<nucleusConnect>/connect/auth?response_type=code&client_id=<blazeServerClientId>&redirect_uri=<identityRedirectUri>`
+   from the preAuth `CONF` (a missing key → null string → crash `0x961554`/`0x9614a4`), GETs it over plain
+   HTTP with its PSN ticket in a `psn_ticket` header (base64), follows the 302 to `redirect_uri?code=…` and
+   logs in with **Authentication2 (35) login (10)** `{AUTH = code, EXTB = online id, EXTI}`. The server
+   points `nucleusConnect` at its own HTTP server (`http://<server IP>:80`, already tunneled by the bridge's
+   `skate3` preset), `/connect/auth` swaps the ticket for a one-time code (`NucleusAuth`), and the
+   Authentication2 login runs the PS3 login with that ticket (`Ps3LoginHandler.Login`). Unanswered, 35/10
+   times out after 11 s and Madden logs out (Authentication 70 = logout) with "EA servers not available".
+3. **OSDKSettings group `SG_MATCHUP`.** Madden opens it right after login and looks up one view per match
+   type (`QM_STD … CS_MUTDT`, name table `0x2335440`, read by `0x14fa5dc`); a missing view crashes at
+   `0x14fa760`. Served with those views and no settings. It uses NHL's `O_SG_*` groups too.
+
+Then: "Tuning Data Update — an error has occurred" (the tuning download `DP_TUNING_URL` isn't served;
+answer No to retrying) → **Madden's main menu online** (HOME/PLAY/SHARE/CUSTOMIZE, Online Head to Head
+tile). Its Madden-specific settings (`OSDK_MADSET` config: `DP_*_URL`, `TILE_*`, `MM_*`, ...) are still
+served empty.
+
+How this was found: `USCL_LOGPOINTS` (interpreter, offline): `*cfgLookup@r4` on the config lookup printed
+every key Madden asked for; a logpoint on the preAuth callback (`0xa39b3c`) showed `r5 = 0` (success) —
+together they pointed at the map order. Madden's EBOOT: `xorriso -extract /PS3_GAME/USRDIR/EBOOT.BIN`,
+`rpcs3 --decrypt`; code and data both map at file offset + 0x10000. Its TDF reflection is laid out
+`vtable, "<Name>_CLONE_\0<Name>\0Blaze::…::<Name>"`; the member table getter is the word before `_CLONE_`.
 
 ### Disassembly toolchain (reusable for any PS3 game)
 
